  "plain": {
    "what": "Bitcoin is digital money that lives online, and its price jumps up and down a lot. On October 2 it hit US$87,249.05, and by the first week of November it had dropped to about US$75,600, its lowest price in seven weeks. At that low, each dollar got you about 15% more bitcoin than at the high.",
    "so_what": "Say you put in $10,000 at the low instead of the high. That 15% works out to about $1,500 more coin, but the extra coin only helps if the price climbs back, and nobody knows if it will.",
    "do": "Open your app and write down whether your weekly money went in during the first week of November.",
    "words": [
      {
        "term": "bitcoin",
        "means": "digital money that lives online, with a price that swings a lot"
      },
      {
        "term": "spot price",
        "means": "the price right now, if you paid today"
      },
      {
        "term": "7-week low",
        "means": "the lowest price in the last seven weeks"
      },
      {
        "term": "weekly buy",
        "means": "money your app puts in for you every week, on its own"
      },
      {
        "term": "US$ and CAD",
        "means": "US dollars and Canadian dollars, which are worth different amounts"
      },
      {
        "term": "exchange rate",
        "means": "how many Canadian dollars it takes to get one US dollar"
      },
      {
        "term": "recover",
        "means": "the price climbs back up to where it was"
      }
    ]
  },
  "caption": "🐶⛏️ If you hit pause on bitcoin, $1,500 of coin might've slipped by.\n\nBitcoin slid in early November, so weekly buys that kept going got about 15% more coin per dollar than at the high. That only helps if the price climbs back, and nobody knows if it will.\n\nComment PAUSE and I'll send you the pause cost table 🪙\nDid yours keep going?\n\nDig #N · a Toronto chihuahua on the road to $1M\n#bitcoincanada #cryptocanada #torontofinance",
  "caption_b": "🐶⛏️ What happens if your weekly bitcoin buy kept running through the 7-week low?\n\nBitcoin slid to about US$75,600 in early November, so every weekly buy that kept running got more coin per dollar. That only pays off if the price climbs back, and nobody knows if it will.\n\nComment PAUSE and I'll send you my pause cost table 🪙\nDid yours keep running?\n\nDig #N · a Toronto chihuahua on the road to $1M\n#bitcoincanada #cryptocanada #torontofinance",
  "caption_family": "curious"
